Subject: Assign The C-Function Frame Argument Buffer

What this does
  js_call_c_function_data and js_call_c_closure never assign sf->arg_buf, so
  the JSStackFrame they publish to rt->current_stack_frame carries whatever the
  C stack held while the callee re-enters the engine.

Why we need it
  sf is a C-stack local. Nothing in the shipping engine reads arg_buf for these
  frame kinds, but any consumer that walks frames precisely -- a root scanner,
  or a debugger inspecting C-function frames -- reads it immediately.

What it adds
  Both sites assign sf->arg_buf before calling their callee, matching
  js_call_c_function. The publish order is unchanged: no engine code runs
  between the publish and these stores.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -7765,6 +7765,7 @@
     sf->is_constructor = (flags & JS_CALL_FLAG_CONSTRUCTOR) != 0;
     sf->cur_func = unsafe_unconst(func_obj);
     sf->arg_count = argc;
+    sf->arg_buf = (JSValue *)arg_buf;
     ret = s->func(ctx, this_val, argc, arg_buf, s->magic, vc(s->data));
     rt->current_stack_frame = sf->prev_frame;
     return ret;
@@ -7891,6 +7892,7 @@
     sf->is_constructor = (flags & JS_CALL_FLAG_CONSTRUCTOR) != 0;
     sf->cur_func = unsafe_unconst(func_obj);
     sf->arg_count = argc;
+    sf->arg_buf = (JSValue *)arg_buf;
     ret = s->func(ctx, this_val, argc, arg_buf, s->magic, s->opaque);
     rt->current_stack_frame = sf->prev_frame;
 
